WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.996 --> 00:00:15.439
As left the chamber where the murdered king lay, he met Lady Macbeth in the hallway.

2
00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:17.920
She had been too anxious to sleep.

3
00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.681
"I have done the deed," he said.

4
00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:24.942
Then looking at her, he whispered, "Didn't you hear a noise?

5
00:00:25.462 --> 00:00:28.043
One of Duncan's servants I thought he was awake.

6
00:00:29.063 --> 00:00:32.744
He mumbled, ‘God bless us,' as if he were praying in his sleep.

7
00:00:33.832 --> 00:00:36.894
I should have said, ‘Amen,' but the word stuck in my throat.

8
00:00:37.755 --> 00:00:39.416
I was so much in need of a blessing!

9
00:00:39.916 --> 00:00:41.177
Why couldn't I say ‘Amen'?"

10
00:00:41.958 --> 00:00:46.801
Then, looking at his bloody dagger, he whispered, "This is a sorry sight."

11
00:00:48.582 --> 00:00:49.803
"What are you doing with that?"

12
00:00:50.543 --> 00:00:51.624
Lady Macbeth gasped.

13
00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:52.785
"Go back!

14
00:00:53.365 --> 00:00:56.427
Leave the dagger by the servants, and cover them with blood."

15
00:00:57.628 --> 00:00:58.649
Macbeth shook his head.

16
00:00:58.669 --> 00:01:01.230
"I'll go no more.

17
00:01:01.791 --> 00:01:03.232
I don't dare look at what I've done."

18
00:01:04.436 --> 00:01:08.279
Without hesitating, Lady Macbeth took the dagger and hurried back to the king's room.

19
00:01:09.379 --> 00:01:11.741
When she returned, her hands were covered in blood.

20
00:01:12.622 --> 00:01:16.044
"Now my hands are the same color as yours," she said.

21
00:01:16.064 --> 00:01:20.467
"Quickly, let's go wash this filthy evidence from our hands."

22
00:01:21.507 --> 00:01:25.250
In the pale light of dawn, there was a loud knocking on the great gate of the castle.

23
00:01:26.391 --> 00:01:32.675
Macduff, who was the thane of Fife and one of Duncan's most trusted noblemen, had arrived to accompany

24
00:01:32.695 --> 00:01:34.196
the king on his journey that day.

25
00:01:35.112 --> 00:01:40.015
The gatekeeper, who had drunk too much wine the night before, rose from his post and rubbed his

26
00:01:40.136 --> 00:01:40.696
aching head.

27
00:01:40.716 --> 00:01:45.899
"The gatekeeper of hell couldn't be more miserable than me.

28
00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:50.182
In the name of the devil," he called, "who's there?"

29
00:01:51.443 --> 00:01:55.506
Macbeth, who had heard the knocking on the gate, arrived to welcome Macduff.

30
00:01:56.587 --> 00:02:01.170
As they walked to the king's chamber, Macbeth kept silent, but Macduff talked eagerly.

31
00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:05.256
"I can't remember such an evil night," he said.

32
00:02:05.276 --> 00:02:08.878
"At our camp, a cold wind kept blowing the fire out.

33
00:02:09.919 --> 00:02:13.421
After we fell asleep, our horses broke loose and ran wild with fear.

34
00:02:14.641 --> 00:02:19.864
I don't know what upset them, but the birds, too, it seemed, were flying madly and screeching all

35
00:02:19.904 --> 00:02:24.487
night." "Yes, it was a rough night," Macbeth said solemnly.

36
00:02:25.447 --> 00:02:29.409
They arrived at the king's chamber, and Macbeth let Macduff go in ahead of him.

37
00:02:29.429 --> 00:02:30.970
"O horror!

38
00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:34.372
Horror!" Macduff cried when he saw Duncan.

39
00:02:34.952 --> 00:02:37.034
"My tongue cannot speak the horror!"

40
00:02:37.934 --> 00:02:43.138
He left the room to wake the other noblemen, calling out, "Murder and treason!"

41
00:02:43.838 --> 00:02:48.441
So Macbeth stood alone, staring at the sleeping servants that his wife had smeared with blood.

42
00:02:49.482 --> 00:02:52.044
Outside the room, Banquo and Ross came running.

43
00:02:52.864 --> 00:02:57.127
Lady Macbeth came hurrying too, and Duncan's two sons were the last to arrive.

44
00:02:57.147 --> 00:02:59.008
"What is the matter?"

45
00:02:59.549 --> 00:03:01.170
asked Malcolm, the king's older son.

46
00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:05.445
"Your royal father has been murdered," said Macduff.

47
00:03:05.465 --> 00:03:07.126
"By who?"

48
00:03:08.066 --> 00:03:09.007
cried Donaldbain.

49
00:03:09.988 --> 00:03:12.990
"By the servants in his chamber," said Macduff.

50
00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:14.791
"Or so it seems.

51
00:03:15.412 --> 00:03:19.795
A bloody dagger lies between them and their hands and faces are covered in blood."

52
00:03:20.735 --> 00:03:24.878
While Macduff was describing the scene, Macbeth came out of the gruesome chamber.

53
00:03:24.898 --> 00:03:32.984
"Forgive my fury," he said, looking them all in the eye, "but anyone who loved the king and

54
00:03:33.024 --> 00:03:38.168
has a heart of courage would have done the same as I I've killed the guilty servants!"

55
00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:44.614
News of the king's death spread quickly, and many anxious discussions were held throughout the castle.

56
00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:50.098
Not everyone believed that the two servants were to blame, while some thought that they had been paid

57
00:03:50.138 --> 00:03:50.498
to do it.

58
00:03:51.639 --> 00:03:56.143
Malcolm and Donaldbain feared that whoever killed their father would try to kill them next.

59
00:03:56.884 --> 00:04:01.988
They met secretly that night and decided to flee: Malcolm to England and Donaldbain to Ireland.

60
00:04:03.104 --> 00:04:06.885
When people learned that Duncan's sons had fled, many began to suspect them.

61
00:04:08.526 --> 00:04:14.127
After the funeral, with no one from Duncan's family left to take the throne, Macbeth was crowned king.

62
00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:21.229
Macbeth and Lady Macbeth moved to the king's palace at Forres, where they decided to hold a banquet

63
00:04:21.289 --> 00:04:22.350
for all their noblemen.

64
00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:28.071
At Macbeth's request, Banquo and his young son arrived early to meet with the new royal couple.

65
00:04:29.091 --> 00:04:34.550
Macbeth and Banquo talked casually, and Macbeth suggested to Banquo that he go for a ride with his

66
00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:35.370
son before dinner.

67
00:04:36.371 --> 00:04:39.333
As Banquo walked to the stables with his son, he felt anxious.

68
00:04:39.353 --> 00:04:46.317
"I worry that Macbeth got the crown through foul play," he thought, "and yet the witches foretold it

69
00:04:46.457 --> 00:04:48.118
all." He looked at his son.

70
00:04:48.138 --> 00:04:50.879
"Perhaps I will be the father of kings."

71
00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:56.763
Walking quickly through the palace, Macbeth was also thinking of the witches' prophecy about Banquo.

72
00:04:57.703 --> 00:04:58.604
He clenched his fists.

73
00:04:59.548 --> 00:05:01.609
"Why should I have to wear a fruitless crown?

74
00:05:02.349 --> 00:05:05.070
I can't sleep at night; I keep hearing voices.

75
00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:07.852
‘Macbeth shall sleep no more!'

76
00:05:08.172 --> 00:05:08.612
they say.

77
00:05:08.632 --> 00:05:11.073
‘Macbeth has murdered sleep!'

78
00:05:11.533 --> 00:05:15.935
Did I commit murder and corrupt my mind just so that Banquo's descendants could be kings?

79
00:05:16.695 --> 00:05:19.577
To be king is nothing, unless I am safely king!"

80
00:05:20.077 --> 00:05:22.278
He arrived at a small hidden door near the stables.

81
00:05:23.378 --> 00:05:25.239
Waiting for him there were two rough men.

82
00:05:26.199 --> 00:05:30.422
He whispered instructions to them, telling them where Banquo and his son would be riding.

83
00:05:30.442 --> 00:05:34.145
"Report back to me when they're dead," he said.

84
00:05:34.886 --> 00:05:39.991
The banquet hall was full that evening, and the tables were crowded when Macbeth and Lady Macbeth entered.

85
00:05:40.991 --> 00:05:46.316
As the guests rose from their seats to bow, she whispered to her husband, "Be bright and happy

86
00:05:46.376 --> 00:05:47.497
among our guests tonight.

87
00:05:48.238 --> 00:05:50.319
You spend too much time alone worrying.

88
00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:52.822
All your worries should have died with Duncan."

89
00:05:52.842 --> 00:05:58.458
"You don't understand," he said quietly as they walked to the head table.

90
00:05:58.478 --> 00:06:03.302
"My mind crawls with scorpions knowing that Banquo and his son are still alive.

91
00:06:04.203 --> 00:06:06.525
But I have arranged a dreadful deed."

92
00:06:07.386 --> 00:06:12.410
She looked at him questioningly, but all he said was, "You will applaud when it's done."

93
00:06:13.011 --> 00:06:17.274
During the banquet, Macbeth went from table to table, conversing with his guests.

94
00:06:18.275 --> 00:06:23.620
Many commented on Banquo's absence, and Macbeth replied that he missed his friend and hoped he would arrive

95
00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:28.391
soon. Suddenly, he noticed two men skulking at the doorway to the hall.

96
00:06:28.831 --> 00:06:33.135
He knew it was the assassins, returned from their task, and he went quickly to meet them.

97
00:06:33.155 --> 00:06:36.377
"There's blood on your face," he said.

98
00:06:36.397 --> 00:06:40.661
"It's Banquo's, then," answered the first murderer.

99
00:06:40.681 --> 00:06:41.662
"He's dead."

100
00:06:41.682 --> 00:06:43.844
"Good. And his son?"

101
00:06:44.444 --> 00:06:45.005
asked Macbeth.

102
00:06:45.445 --> 00:06:50.529
But Banquo's son had escaped, and when Macbeth heard this, he went into a rage and sent the

103
00:06:50.569 --> 00:06:51.350
murderers away.

104
00:06:52.451 --> 00:06:53.852
Lady Macbeth came out to get him.

105
00:06:54.792 --> 00:06:59.074
"My lord," she said, "your guests notice your absence."

106
00:07:00.074 --> 00:07:05.777
They returned to take their seats, but as they approached their chairs, Macbeth's face went white and he

107
00:07:05.817 --> 00:07:06.577
began to tremble.

108
00:07:07.097 --> 00:07:07.637
"What is it?"

109
00:07:07.897 --> 00:07:08.338
she asked.

110
00:07:08.778 --> 00:07:09.458
"Please, sit."

111
00:07:10.378 --> 00:07:16.401
Staring at his chair as if something unimaginably horrible were seated there, Macbeth yelled, "Don't look at me

112
00:07:16.461 --> 00:07:18.121
with your wounded and gory face!"

113
00:07:19.182 --> 00:07:20.142
The hall went silent.

114
00:07:20.883 --> 00:07:22.323
All the guests stopped and stared.

115
00:07:22.343 --> 00:07:24.004
"See there!

116
00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:26.321
Behold," Macbeth cried.

117
00:07:26.341 --> 00:07:27.881
"Can't you see!

118
00:07:28.462 --> 00:07:31.703
Look! He should be dead, but there he sits!"

119
00:07:32.723 --> 00:07:35.184
Hastily, Lady Macbeth turned to the guests.

120
00:07:35.785 --> 00:07:37.866
"Please, excuse my lord," she said.

121
00:07:37.886 --> 00:07:39.666
"He is not well.

122
00:07:40.146 --> 00:07:43.448
This is just a momentary fit and will soon pass."

123
00:07:44.128 --> 00:07:45.249
She grabbed her husband's arm.

124
00:07:45.269 --> 00:07:46.529
"Are you mad?

125
00:07:46.909 --> 00:07:48.370
You stare at nothing but a chair."

126
00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:53.552
"As sure as I am standing here, I saw him," Macbeth said.

127
00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:59.252
"With his dead eyes, and bleeding from his gaping wounds, it was Banquo's ghost!"
